<title>USA: Chiron makes FDA filing for wound agent.</title>
<headline>Chiron makes FDA filing for wound agent.</headline>
<dateline>EMERYVILLE, Calif. 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chiron Corp said on Thursday that it and Johnson and Johnson filed biologics licensing applications for their Regranex Gel wound healing agent with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration.</p>
<p>Chiron manufactures the agent from recombinant human platelet-derived growth factor into Regranex, the company said.</p>
<p>Johnson and Johnson will market the product, Chiron said.</p>
